Practical NO: 3

Aim :-

File Handling Operations: Create and manage files.

Theory :-

Linux provides various commands to create, view, copy, move and delete files, making file management easy through the terminal.

Requirement:

•Linux Operating system
•Linux terminal
•Text files for performing file handling operations.
•Basic knowledge of Linux file commands.

Command explanation :- 

a) Create files using touch

$ touch filename.txt : creates a new empty file with the specified name.

b) View file contents using cat, more, less

$ cat filename.txt : Display the complete contents of a file.

$ more filename.txt : Displays the contents of a file one screen at a time.

$ less filename.txt : Displays file contents page by page and allow scrolling.

c) Copy and move files using cp, mv

$ cp source.txt destination.txt : creates a copy of the source file with the specified destination name.

$ mv oldname.txt newname.txt : Moves or renames a file.

d) Delete files using rm

$ rm filename.txt : Permanently removes the specified file from the directory.

